@startuml sequence-sale-posting
' What happens when a sale is confirmed.
title Confirming a sale — stock and books move together

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #55606E
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBorderColor #9AA5B1
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F9FB
  LifeLineBorderColor #C3CCD6
}

actor User
participant "Documents" as DS
participant "Stock" as SS
participant "Accounting" as AS
database PostgreSQL as DB

User -> DS : Confirm this sale

group One database transaction
  DS -> SS : take the goods out of stock
  SS -> DB : record a stock movement

  DS -> DB : mark the sale confirmed

  DS -> AS : record the money side
  AS -> AS : check debit = credit
  AS -> DB : write the accounting entry
end

DS --> User : Sale confirmed

note over SS, AS
  If anything fails — not enough stock,
  or an entry that does not balance —
  the whole thing is undone and
  nothing is saved.
end note

note over DB
  Nothing is ever deleted.
  Cancelling a sale writes an
  opposite movement and an
  opposite entry instead.
end note

@enduml
